# The build context is the repository root (deploy/compose.yml and
# service-kit/docker/compose/service.yml both say `context` .. to it), and the
# Dockerfile COPYs whole trees -- `src/${SERVICE_PACKAGE}`, `service-kit/vendor/`,
# `migrations`. Without this file a LOCAL build carries whatever the working tree
# holds beside the source: bytecode, virtualenvs, tool caches. Bytecode is the one
# that changes behaviour: a mutant restored within the same second at the same size
# leaves a .pyc whose header still matches the restored source, so an image built
# for a mutation proof's "restore" arm ran the mutant (measured in llm-gateway,
# an earlier change). CI checkouts are clean, so this protects local proof, not
# production bytes -- and it keeps both built from the same inputs.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
.venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
.git
